<description>&lt;p&gt;Linares, a former Venezuelan world champion boxer, was detained by US immigration officials while a gay man was appointed Venezuela's foreign minister, showing internal political shifts. Uruguay President Yamandú Orsi was accused by Venezuela of interference after calling for free elections, and a special forces soldier who bet $400,000 on Maduro's removal made his first court appearance. A marine died after going overboard in the first US military operation in the Caribbean, and the ousted leader Nicolas Maduro is scheduled to stand trial on June 1, 2027. The United States is Venezuela's biggest oil buyer as the Hormuz crisis and Maduro's ouster accelerate change, and there were 2 battle-related deaths in 2007, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxNNXIyMjB0bmNDczNUZ2dldlNWWmJuZlFBX0lhZmJWVThuWVFIVlIzN2dDSXU2ai1QVTFjemxKQ2hENkUxZEFtekl6WktjazBKSkhocWZJRm5fXzZ6MFFGU052ZVpaWWNiaHNudkpRMTM1MUF6akdZOXp3azg0RkNxaUY2VUZTSV9JbWlUU2hGOF91WkcxQXV2NmRGZGpDbHZEbG9YejMwZjV6dkZ3Mm5LRHMwaDdnZzVLS2R5bw?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiswFBVV95cUxQVUJGTmU0OUlnNHg1QVdVRUZsQVZkMWZ2MzhqRFBIMzFxOUNpN3AtUUl6a1lSZnNnZ3hpbUJUeFNqLS1mNlJtVHJtRk1UZFhNNmU1X0ZkS083UEF1S3F1TUJHS0tOaF9PalpmVEJMZjg2blpsRHVHeU05enVwakI2cFc0LXhmM3loeWotMkNyVGxsZEh5VVhxeDNZQzJtdnRlMGZaMGxiYXp3V0JnZWFwT2ZzYw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiigFBVV95cUxOVkoxOExpb2FwVUotZ0dnU0RPbWotTF96M2tKaDZmM09kOW5hclBRb04zUGlUUkVtdEplTzNlODBLbUFKTWNUeUdjRWF0Q2Z3LWx2ZXJNN3ltOHpxckVvUU01OUExX0RzNDhIRUlxUFJycXUxYW1mWjRJLTY2V0g5QjNadUprUFUzcXc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Watermark Out News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxNSEtzWjJEUHF2OTZka0Q3Ri03ZzRIMnZ0bC1TeWhRem